en:
So, we're finally down to the last story, huh.
The seventh one still hasn't shown up after all this time...
I wonder if they forgot.{p}

Mr. Kondo wouldn't see her at school, so she looked up his address and lay in wait outside the apartment where he lived alone.
Women in love are scary, huh?
Mr. Kondo was at his wits' end, and in the end he even got down on his hands and knees and begged, apparently.{p}

Just then, Mr. Kondo felt eyes on his back.
A cold gaze that stabbed right into him.
With a bad feeling, he slowly turned around...{p}

And there was Hirai.
Leaning against the faculty room door, she was glaring coldly at Mr. Kondo from the shadows.
And when their eyes met, she suddenly ran away.{p}

For whatever reason, Hirai ran into the gym.
Thinking about it later, maybe she was luring Mr. Kondo the whole time.
I mean, as fast as Hirai was, if she'd really wanted to get away, she could have easily.{p}

With that, Hirai suddenly pulled out a knife.
"...Wh-what are you doing?"
Mr. Kondo was startled.{p}

With the knife stuck into the base, she twisted it around, digging and gouging.
And she did it with a blank face, as if she felt nothing at all.
The one who was shocked was Mr. Kondo.{p}

"Ah... AAAAAAAAAGH!"
Mr. Kondo must have been really scared, I think.
He mustered the last of his strength and ran.{p}

"Gwegh!"
You could almost hear his thick lips ripping away, flesh and all.
Prying his mouth open with a strength you'd never believe came from a woman, Hirai poured the whole bowlful of needles into it.{p}

You want to get married soon, right?
That works out perfectly, then.
Hirai's really beautiful, too.{p}

Even if you say you don't want to get married, you can't stay like that your whole life.
...Right?
And Hirai's really beautiful, too.{p}

Hirai couldn't take it and ran away.
Without the slightest idea why Sato had said such a thing.
She was so mortified she couldn't stand it.{p}

"It's not like I'm going to kill you or anything..."
As she said it, a strange light gleamed in her eyes.
She started wandering in a daze again.{p}

In the room where she'd been changing, a bright red wedding dress was lying on the floor.
The one who found the red dress was Sato.
When he ran over to it in shock, the dress just vanished into thin air, or so the story goes.{p}

This is something Sato talked about later...
He said it felt like he heard a voice coming from somewhere.
And the voice said this, apparently.{p}

Hey, {a}.
What do you think that means...?
...{p}

There was a small trace of blood on the carpet.
"I wonder if this will still work...?"
She snipped off the bloodstained carpet fibers with scissors and tried placing them in the center of the magic circle.{p}

But her hobbies were a bit, well...
Not just a bit, really...
Remember how I told you earlier it's better not to get too into fortune-telling and stuff?{p}

But one day, out of nowhere, her boyfriend started being cold to her.
She was really sad.
So she went to the fortune-telling shop she always went to, to get a reading on what would happen from then on.{p}

"Gyaaaaaaaaah!☆"
A scream rang out from the fortune-telling parlor.
It was Hirai's voice...{p}

There was no sound, but she felt a tiny pop, and a red, bead-like drop spread over her white fingertip.
It fell from her fingertip to the floor, drip, drip.
From where the blood fell, thin wisps of white smoke began to rise, swaying and drifting as if to cling to Hirai's body.{p}

"Oh my, so you want to quit?"
The fortune-teller was still grinning, just as before.
But then that smile slid away, and{p}

"And you said you were prepared.
That won't do at all.
Telling lies like that!"{p}

For a while after that, Hirai went through some painful days.
Why? Because she could hardly ever see Tanaka.
At school, something always got in the way and she couldn't even catch a glimpse of his face, and when she finally got to see him after school, he'd be with his new girlfriend...{p}

There's a better way than casting curses. You'd do better to polish yourself more, she said.
And she promised Hirai she would make her even more beautiful.
To do that, the fortune-teller said, she needed Hirai's nails this time.{p}

She pulled something glinting out of her pocket.
It was a box cutter.
And she slid her arm around Suzuki's back, and from behind...{p}

Normally that would've been enough for her to give up, but Suzuki had asked her out once, right?
Even though it was gone in an instant.
That made her even sadder.{p}

Hmm.
Personality next, huh.
So looks don't matter to you at all?{p}

Nope, that's not it.
Not an incoming first-year.
It was a new teacher.{p}

"I-I forgot☆
I've forgotten all about that☆"
Mr. Kondo screamed at the top of his lungs.{p}

There was no one outside the door.
He let out a sigh of relief.
But just as he went to close the door...{p}

Then Hirai yanked hard on Mr. Kondo's arm.
She was trying to drag him outside.
Mr. Kondo fought back desperately.{p}

With his own arm still sticking outside, he tried to slam the door again and again.
"Uwaaagh☆
Uwaaagh☆"{p}

Mr. Kondo's arm was caught in the door, and a dull crunch echoed all around.
Maybe he didn't even know what he was doing.
He was just so terrified of her...{p}
